{
  "dom_id": "step-q96873",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/131d9f30fac5b1cc4b8eb72a989ca16b0d3cbf7d16725aa38581bfd115b1fc77.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(1,-2)$, $(-1,2),$ $(-4,8).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/87d2a7f522d68e1a50d9c5bb5e33498b2a28e869785f5109c4f6bf3a1c7ff701.png)",
